{
  "id": "m25l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Enumeraciones con Enum",
    "en": "Enumerations with Enum"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Constantes con nombre"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Un **Enum** agrupa constantes relacionadas bajo nombres claros, en vez de usar números 'mágicos' sueltos por el código."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from enum import Enum",
          "",
          "class Color(Enum):",
          "    ROJO = 1",
          "    VERDE = 2",
          "    AZUL = 3",
          "",
          "print(Color.ROJO)",
          "print(Color.ROJO.value)",
          "print(Color.ROJO.name)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Color.ROJO",
          "1",
          "ROJO"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Si no te importa el valor concreto, `auto()` los asigna por ti (empezando en 1)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from enum import Enum, auto",
          "",
          "class Dia(Enum):",
          "    LUNES = auto()",
          "    MARTES = auto()"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Los enums hacen el código más legible y evitan errores: `Color.ROJO` se entiende mejor que un 1 suelto."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Named constants"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "An **Enum** groups related constants under clear names, instead of scattering 'magic' numbers through the code."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from enum import Enum",
          "",
          "class Color(Enum):",
          "    ROJO = 1",
          "    VERDE = 2",
          "    AZUL = 3",
          "",
          "print(Color.ROJO)",
          "print(Color.ROJO.value)",
          "print(Color.ROJO.name)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Color.ROJO",
          "1",
          "ROJO"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "If you don't care about the exact value, `auto()` assigns them for you (starting at 1)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from enum import Enum, auto",
          "",
          "class Dia(Enum):",
          "    LUNES = auto()",
          "    MARTES = auto()"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Enums make code more readable and avoid errors: `Color.ROJO` reads better than a lone 1."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m25l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define un Enum `Color` con ROJO=1, VERDE=2 y AZUL=3.",
        "en": "Define an Enum `Color` with ROJO=1, VERDE=2 and AZUL=3."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from enum import Enum",
        "",
        "# define el Enum Color"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from enum import Enum",
        "",
        "class Color(Enum):",
        "    ROJO = 1",
        "    VERDE = 2",
        "    AZUL = 3"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Hereda de Enum y asigna un valor a cada nombre."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Inherit from Enum and assign a value to each name."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "Color",
          "harness": "assert Color.ROJO.value == 1\nassert Color.VERDE.name == 'VERDE'\nassert isinstance(Color.AZUL, Color)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m25l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define un Enum `Dia` con LUNES, MARTES y MIERCOLES usando `auto()` (sus valores serán 1, 2 y 3).",
        "en": "Define an Enum `Dia` with LUNES, MARTES and MIERCOLES using `auto()` (values will be 1, 2 and 3)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from enum import Enum, auto",
        "",
        "# define el Enum Dia"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from enum import Enum, auto",
        "",
        "class Dia(Enum):",
        "    LUNES = auto()",
        "    MARTES = auto()",
        "    MIERCOLES = auto()"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "auto() asigna 1, 2, 3... en orden."
        ],
        "en": [
          "auto() assigns 1, 2, 3... in order."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "Dia",
          "harness": "assert Dia.LUNES.value == 1\nassert Dia.MARTES.value == 2\nassert Dia.MIERCOLES.value == 3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}